Restore the OEM app-feature/cust config-file locator the v3.0 bring-up stubbed to
return empty (which also starved com.oplus.aiunit's AssetsUnitStore.listFilesFromOS).
Enumerate the LOS partitions (/system_ext,/product,/system,/vendor,/odm)+<configName>
instead of the absent OEM /my_* cust partitions.

(cherry picked from commit dbbebac87c7a1b5a48e7e10ba9a87d11e191f878)

Ledger: hardware_oplus.md Accepted Group C row 2 (dbbebac8)
Stub-matrix: task-9-stub-inventory.md row K03 — consumer: OEM app-feature scan / gallery motion-photo replay gate (empty stub broke it, v3.1 fix); location: oplus-fwk boot jar, depends on c009c8d2; lands in the same series as 5d340832 (K01 isPermit) per the v3.1/v3.2 bootloop pairing
Change-Id: I75a3ba96906cec4da4bc36fd48ada5e62ed5f60f
---
 .../com/oplus/cust/OplusCfgFilePolicy.java    | 20 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/oplus-fwk/src/com/oplus/cust/OplusCfgFilePolicy.java b/oplus-fwk/src/com/oplus/cust/OplusCfgFilePolicy.java
index 49ced32d..7d2fcd1e 100644
--- a/oplus-fwk/src/com/oplus/cust/OplusCfgFilePolicy.java
+++ b/oplus-fwk/src/com/oplus/cust/OplusCfgFilePolicy.java
@@ -27,8 +27,26 @@ public class OplusCfgFilePolicy {
         return new ArrayList();
     }
 
+    // OOS maps <configName> onto the OEM cust levels (/my_product, /my_carrier, ... + base),
+    // which are absent on LineageOS. Enumerate the LOS partition layout instead so the OEM
+    // AppFeatureProvider / cust consumers locate their config dirs the same way OOS does —
+    // e.g. /system_ext/etc/extension/com.oplus.app-features.xml. Returns the existing
+    // <partition><configName> dirs in priority order; empty only when none exist, which keeps
+    // consumers-with-no-config degrading gracefully (the reason the port stubbed this to empty).
     public static List getCfgLevelList(String configName, int slot) {
-        return new ArrayList();
+        List list = new ArrayList();
+        if (configName == null) {
+            return list;
+        }
+        String sub = configName.startsWith("/") ? configName : "/" + configName;
+        String[] roots = { "/system_ext", "/product", "/system", "/vendor", "/odm" };
+        for (String root : roots) {
+            String dir = root + sub;
+            if (new File(dir).isDirectory()) {
+                list.add(dir);
+            }
+        }
+        return list;
     }
 
     public static File getCfgTopPriorityFile(String configName, String dir, int slot) {
